WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.636
-Hey, everyone.
Tonight is our 1,000th show.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.972
In a different time,
you could have expected

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.741
an evening filled with
celebrity guests

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.442
and looks back at
our funniest moments.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.278
Instead, it's a
one-man extratticganza.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.880
[ Foghorn blows ]

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.548
I don't know -- maybe
at the end, to celebrate,

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.417
my kids will come out and say,
"This has been 'A Closer Look.'"

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.552
I guess you'll just have to
stick around and find out.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.154
Anyway, the extratticganza
must go on.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:24.056
President Trump's
political standing is as

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:25.758
weak as it's ever been,
so he's decided

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.361
to pin his hopes for a comeback
on whining about polls

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:31.631
and sticking up for
the...Confederacy?

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.733
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.804
♪♪

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.605
As his poll numbers
continue to fall

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.941
and he descends deeper
into political desperation,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.811
President Trump is as
fixated as ever on things

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.046
he sees on TV
that make him feel bad,

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.914
like, for example,
a new CNN poll

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:51.750
that puts his
job approval rating at 38%

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.286
and has him losing to
Joe Biden by 14 points.

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.555
Now, the president's job
approval is tracked constantly,

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:58.591
and especially
in an election year,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.992
new polls come out all the time.

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:04.430
So obsessing over any one poll
is mostly a waste of time,

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.832
which is exactly why Trump
is doing it,

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.400
because the guy loves
to waste time.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.835
It's the only thing
he's good at.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.936
His favorite sport
takes five hours to play

00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:13.072
and makes drying paint
look like a fireworks show.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.942
And when he's not golfing,
he's glued to the TV,

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.976
which might explain why
his brain, long ago,

00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:19.212
melted into rice pudding.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.247
The human mind just wasn't built

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.349
to withstand that much Hannity.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.418
Humans evolved
from hunter-gatherers.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.620
Trump evolved from a
Cro-Magnon who spent the day

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.558
staring at a cave painting of an
angrier Cro-Magnon.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.626
Just yesterday, Trump tweeted,
"Incredible!

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.962
Fox News just took Congressional
hearing off the air

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.498
just prior to important
witness statements.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.633
More like CNN. Fox is lost."

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:44.503
He tweeted that at 10:56 a.m.
on Wednesday.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.673
Why are you watching TV at
11:00 a.m. on a Wednesday?

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.776
Did you get furloughed
and not tell anyone?

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.644
[ As Trump ] The good news is,
I still have my health insurance

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.080
and, you know,
all the money I stole."

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.548
[ Normal voice ]
There are mass demonstrations

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.884
in the streets
against systemic racism.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.586
police are beating
peaceful protesters,

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.919
a pandemic is still raging,

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:03.422
and tens of millions of people
have lost their jobs,

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.858
and the president is
live-tweeting cable news

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:07.860
in the middle of a workday
like a high-school sophomore

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.228
playing hooky from school.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.631
In fact, even
a high-school sophomore

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.899
would know better than to tweet,

00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:16.035
"I pretended to be sick today
so I could stay home

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.570
and watch 'Price is Right'

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.204
@PrincipalSimms."

00:02:19.204 --> 00:02:21.641
And now the president,
who's obviously anxious

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.009
about his political standing,
apparently has so much free time

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:26.378
on his hands that
he's watching cable news

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:27.980
and getting mad at polls.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.382
-Brand-new CNN poll
hot off the press.

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:34.287
It shows a huge drop in
the president's approval rating

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.055
in just one month,
down 7 points.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.791
It also shows former
vice president Joe Biden

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:43.662
opening up his biggest lead yet,
14 points, over President Trump.

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:47.366
-The Trump campaign is
actually demanding that CNN

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:50.369
retract and actually apologize
for our recent poll

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.438
that shows the president
is trailing

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.874
the presumptive Democratic
presidential nominee,

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.842
the former vice president,
Joe Biden.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.311
-Why does that upset you?

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.812
You were behind in the polls
to Hillary Clinton,

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.013
and now, thanks to our
dumb electoral college,

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.147
you're president.

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:04.517
You're not the hare.
You're the tortoise.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.386
And your shell is like
a bunker you retreat to --

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:08.454
not because you're scared,

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.023
but because you're doing
an inspection.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.159
This all started when Trump saw
the poll and got so pissed,

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:16.162
he actually asked his pollster
to debunk it, tweeting,

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:18.097
"I have retained
highly respected pollster

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.032
McLaughlin &amp; Associates
to analyze today's

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.801
CNN poll (and others),
which I felt were fake,

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:25.271
based on the incredible
enthusiasm we're receiving.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.672
Read analysis for yourself.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:28.507
This is the same thing
they and the others did

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:31.410
when we defeated crooked
Hillary Clinton in 2016.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.179
They are called
suppression polls

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.347
and are put out to
dampen enthusiasm."

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:37.383
First of all, it must be
the easiest thing in the world

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.753
when Trump retains your services
as a pollster to prove something

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.556
is fake, because you could just
give him a one-page print-out

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.657
that says he was right.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.859
And then if he
asks if there's any data,

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.361
you say, "Yeah, do you
want to see it?",

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.796
knowing full well he'll just
say, "No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:51.864
I trust you. I trust you."

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:52.965
I mean, I'd say it
was free money,

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.167
but, then again,
he never pays anyone.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.601
So it serves you right
for working for him,

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.102
McLaughlin &amp; Associates.

00:03:57.102 --> 00:03:58.504
Trump's political standing

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.073
has eroded considerably
over the past month,

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.675
and he's in a weak position
as any incumbent president

00:04:03.675 --> 00:04:05.612
has ever been in the history
of modern polling.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:09.515
So Trump and his supporters in
the GOP and on right-wing TV

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.619
are resorting to the only
two tactics they have left --

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:16.889
amping up the racism and nursing
deranged cultural grievances.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.625
For example,
after the Army -- the Army --

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:22.228
said they were considering
renaming bases

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.397
that had been named after
Confederate leaders,

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:27.100
who were violent white
supremacists and traitors,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.367
Trump lashed out on Twitter.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.670
And, for some reason,
his White House handed out

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.805
physical copies of his statement

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.139
to reporters in the press room.

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:37.142
-The president is dismissing an
idea under consideration

00:04:37.142 --> 00:04:39.912
by the Pentagon
of renaming bases

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.748
that honor Confederate officers.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.048
-Now, let me just
tell you what happened

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:44.984
in the last few minutes here
to give you a sense of

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.485
how this went down at
The White House.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:49.088
The president, of course, just
tweeted a few moments ago,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:50.555
and then they handed out
a print-out

00:04:50.555 --> 00:04:51.791
of the president's tweet.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.159
The press secretary
came out and also read

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:56.395
the president's tweet,
where he said, in part,

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:59.065
"These monumental
and very powerful bases

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.868
have become part of
a great American heritage

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.236
and a history of
winning victory and freedom."

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.305
He says, "Therefore,
my administration

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.273
will not even consider
the renaming

00:05:08.273 --> 00:05:11.443
of these magnificent and fabled
military installations."

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:14.113
-"Our history as
the greatest nation in the world

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.380
will not be tampered with.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.150
Respect our military."

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.584
So, that was directly
from the president.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.520
We spent some time
working on that.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.322
-I'm not sure that's something
I'd necessarily brag about.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:24.557
It's one paragraph.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.759
From the looks of it,
it's like a 14-size font.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.360
I've seen longer blurbs
on book jackets.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.462
It's like the first draft
of a college essay

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:31.898
that's supposed
to be five pages,

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.200
and instead of writing more,
you just jack up the spacing.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.401
Also, what do you mean they're

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.002
"part of a great
American heritage and a history

00:05:37.002 --> 00:05:38.471
of winning, victory,
and freedom?"

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.808
Confederates famously fought
against America, and they lost.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.709
Since when do we name
military bases

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.778
after people who lost wars
against Americans?

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:48.447
Is there a naval base named
after King George III?

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:51.851
Would you make American soldiers
trade at Fort Il Duce?

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.552
Also, I love this part.

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:56.655
"Magnificent and fabled military
installations."

00:05:56.655 --> 00:06:00.158
Those bases are a lot of things,
but they're not fabled.

00:06:00.158 --> 00:06:01.393
They're really there.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:03.796
We're not talking about an
Aztec city of gold.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.531
"Gather around
and I'll tell you the tale

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.434
of a fabled Ft. Bragg,
a charmless cluster

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.571
of wooden buildings where
men fall from the sky,

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:14.139
wings of nylon."

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:16.142
And, by the way, not only were
Confederate leaders

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:18.176
slavers, traders,
and white supremacists,

00:06:18.176 --> 00:06:19.812
they were also dip[bleep]

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.814
Take general Braxton Bragg,
for example.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.649
Bragg resigned from the
Confederate Army

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.217
after losing a decisive battle.

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:28.387
And on top of that, Bragg was a
jackass and an ass[bleep]

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:30.189
Bragg had such a notoriously
bad temper

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.057
that Union
general Ulysses S. Grant,

00:06:32.057 --> 00:06:34.727
in his memoirs, recalled a story
of one of Bragg's superiors

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.862
admonishing him --
"My God, Mr. Bragg,

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:38.931
you have quarreled with every
officer in the Army,

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.599
and now you're quarreling
with yourself."

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:41.967
No wonder Trump likes him.

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:43.969
He was a racist psycho
who liked to fight with people.

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:45.404
They didn't have
Twitter back then,

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:46.972
but I'm guessing
Bragg's telegrams

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:48.508
would have been right up
Trump's alley.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:51.143
"Dear General Grant,
I have retained

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:54.514
highly respected pollster
McLaughlin &amp; Associates

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.482
to analyze the results of
the Civil War,

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.016
which I felt were fake,

00:06:58.016 --> 00:07:00.385
based on the incredible
enthusiasm we are receiving.

00:07:00.385 --> 00:07:02.288
Lyin' Lincoln is a loser!

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:04.323
Regards, General Bragg.

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:07.527
P.S., I spent a good bit of time
working on this."

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:10.729
I listened to a lot of tapes to
get that impression right.

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:12.030
Trump probably likes him
because he thinks

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.232
he invented bragging.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.101
"You know, before Braxton Bragg,
you just had to

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:17.169
hope people knew
how rich you were

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:18.337
without you telling them.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:20.673
It was a dark time.
It was a very dark time."

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.708
Also, it's worth noting that all
of these Confederate generals

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:24.309
Trump is praising
probably would have hated him.

00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:26.279
I mean, sure,
he's also a racist,

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:27.579
but there's no way they'd
enjoy spending time

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:29.181
with this New York City
blowhard.

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:30.583
If he was at
one of their cotillions,

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:31.984
Trump would have been
glove-slapped

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:33.118
every five minutes.

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:35.120
"For the insult of your
locker-room talk,

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.357
I challenge you to
a duel at dawn, good sir."

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:40.092
[ As Trump ] Well,
I can't do dawn tomorrow.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:42.494
I've already been challenged
to a duel then.

00:07:42.494 --> 00:07:43.796
Does next Wednesday work?"

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:45.297
[ Normal voice ] So,
as he plummets in the polls,

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.399
Trump thinks his ticket to a
political resurgence

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:50.302
is appealing directly to
racists who idolize

00:07:50.302 --> 00:07:51.903
the white-supremacist
Confederacy,

00:07:51.903 --> 00:07:53.439
but he's clearly
facing head winds,

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:55.574
because even the
cultural institutions

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:58.110
you might think of
as occupying conservative end

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.580
of the spectrum are dumping
the Confederate symbols.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.180
The U.S. Navy
has joined the Marines

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.383
in moving to ban the
Confederate battle flag.

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.285
And even NASCAR is weighing in

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.954
with a firm
anti-Confederacy stance.

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:13.158
-On Wednesday, NASCAR officially
banned the Confederate flag

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:16.428
from all events after a request
from Bubba Wallace,

00:08:16.428 --> 00:08:18.197
the sport's lone black driver.

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:21.033
-NASCAR announcing,
"The flag runs contrary

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:22.702
to our commitment
to providing a welcoming

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:25.304
and inclusive environment
for all fans"

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:28.106
and is now "prohibited from
all NASCAR events

00:08:28.106 --> 00:08:30.242
and properties,"
effective immediately.

00:08:30.242 --> 00:08:31.476
-Oh, my God.

00:08:31.476 --> 00:08:35.014
This can only mean one thing --
NASCAR is Antifa.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:36.115
Next thing you know,
they're gonna start wearing

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:37.216
helmets to hide their faces

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:38.918
and attacking people with
glass bottles.

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:40.820
[ Gasps ]

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.455
And I don't know much
about NASCAR,

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:44.723
other than the fact that 38%
of the drivers

00:08:44.723 --> 00:08:46.458
seem to be named Rusty,

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:48.093
but that's an
impressive step to take.

00:08:48.093 --> 00:08:49.361
I applaud you.

00:08:49.361 --> 00:08:51.230
And if some of your fans boo,
maybe you can just

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.798
drown them out by --
I don't know --

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:54.967
driving 50 cars 200 miles
per hour around a track.

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:56.035
That might work.

00:08:56.035 --> 00:08:57.803
Anyway, I honestly
can't even believe

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:59.538
it's a question
at this point whether or not

00:08:59.538 --> 00:09:01.006
we should be
celebrating the symbols of

00:09:01.006 --> 00:09:04.276
an explicitly white-supremacist
cause, like the Confederacy,

00:09:04.276 --> 00:09:06.045
that fought to destroy
the United States.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:09.114
And, yet, NASCAR
is doing more to lead right now

00:09:09.114 --> 00:09:11.316
than the President of
the United States,

00:09:11.316 --> 00:09:13.385
which has to be especially
bruising for Trump,

00:09:13.385 --> 00:09:16.455
because just a few months ago,
he was the grand marshal

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:19.791
at the Daytona 500, even taking
a lap around the track

00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:21.527
in his presidential limo.

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:23.495
So all he did was sit in the car

00:09:23.495 --> 00:09:24.830
while it drove around
in a circle.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.899
Trump even finds ways
to make sports lazy.

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:28.968
That's the least-impressive
political appearance

00:09:28.968 --> 00:09:30.369
at a sporting event since
Chris Christie

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.438
was caught hugging
Jerry Jones at a Cowboys game.

00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:33.805
Also, dude,
you're from New Jersey.

00:09:33.805 --> 00:09:36.275
You have two semi-professional
football teams.

00:09:36.275 --> 00:09:37.643
Just because they suck
doesn't mean

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:38.811
you get to pick another one.

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:41.347
The Knicks suck, but you don't
see Andrew Cuomo

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:43.482
hanging out with Toronto Raptor.

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:45.084
The Right's defense of
Confederate symbols

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:46.752
comes as protestors
across the country

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.353
have been taking down
Confederate statues,

00:09:48.353 --> 00:09:50.456
like, for example, the statue of
Confederate president

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:53.358
and violent white-supremacist
traitor Jefferson Davis

00:09:53.358 --> 00:09:54.727
in Richmond on Wednesday.

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:56.128
This morning,
Trump once again defended

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:59.364
Confederate symbols,
scream-tweeting, in all caps,

00:09:59.364 --> 00:10:02.735
"Those that deny their history
are doomed to repeat it."

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:05.037
Of course, Trump probably most
hates the removal

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:07.539
of Confederate statues
because he stands like

00:10:07.539 --> 00:10:10.209
a statue of Donald Trump that is
currently being pulled down.

00:10:10.209 --> 00:10:13.278
I mean, seriously,
look at that forward lean.

00:10:13.278 --> 00:10:15.648
All that's missing are
protesters pulling on cables.

00:10:15.648 --> 00:10:17.115
"If we could just get
the chest out

00:10:17.115 --> 00:10:18.751
a little further past the toes,

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:20.386
the whole thing will come down."

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:21.921
And, yet,
venerating the Confederacy

00:10:21.921 --> 00:10:24.256
isn't the only insane
culture-war issue

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:26.225
the Right has pinned
their hopes on this week.

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:28.160
Now that Trump has
cratered the economy

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.595
and utterly failed to contain
a pandemic still raging

00:10:30.595 --> 00:10:32.798
across the country,
all the right-wing weirdos

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:38.170
on Fox News have left is to get
mad at cartoons and Muppets.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:41.106
-HBO Max's "Looney Tunes" reboot

00:10:41.106 --> 00:10:43.909
is disarming
some classic characters.

00:10:43.909 --> 00:10:46.411
-What?!
-Elmer Fudd's rifle is gone.

00:10:46.411 --> 00:10:47.646
No more.
-Oh, no.

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:50.249
-Yosemite Sam's 6-irons -- out.
-Six-shots.

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:51.850
-He's been disarmed.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:56.355
-Foot washing, and now Fudd
without the rifle.

00:10:56.355 --> 00:10:59.057
Okay, there...
-Well, it's virtue signaling.

00:10:59.057 --> 00:11:01.093
-Yeah, I'm bringing this sign
to the protest

00:11:01.093 --> 00:11:03.795
at the community center later.

00:11:03.795 --> 00:11:10.869
-Oh. Well, they look upset.
Are the protesters sad?

00:11:10.869 --> 00:11:13.639
-They are sad and upset.

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:16.842
And they have
every right to be, Elmo.

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:19.311
People are upset because racism

00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:22.348
is a huge problem
in our country.

00:11:22.348 --> 00:11:26.118
Across the country,
people of color,

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:28.687
especially in
the black community,

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:30.922
are being treated unfairly

00:11:30.922 --> 00:11:33.025
because of how they look.

00:11:33.025 --> 00:11:36.128
-It's a children's show.
Got that, Bobby?

00:11:36.128 --> 00:11:39.731
America is a very bad place,
and it's your fault.

00:11:39.731 --> 00:11:42.234
So no matter what happens,
no matter what they do to you

00:11:42.234 --> 00:11:45.204
when you grow up,
you have no right to complain.

00:11:45.204 --> 00:11:47.073
That's the message,
and it starts very young.

00:11:47.073 --> 00:11:48.541
-Think of how far
you've fallen in life

00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:50.609
when you're mad at a Muppet.

00:11:50.609 --> 00:11:53.078
I mean, just steaming all day,
barking at your producers,

00:11:53.078 --> 00:11:54.546
"Get me that footage
of Elmo's dad.

00:11:54.546 --> 00:11:57.816
And look into Beaker, too.
He's awfully quiet."

00:11:57.816 --> 00:11:59.685
It's especially surprising
that Tucker is mad

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:01.386
at a children's show,
because for most of his career,

00:12:01.386 --> 00:12:02.754
he dressed like a child.

00:12:02.754 --> 00:12:04.522
You know, he always looked
like the ring bearer

00:12:04.522 --> 00:12:05.857
at a Connecticut wedding.

00:12:05.857 --> 00:12:07.793
"Okay, Tucker,
give them the rings.

00:12:07.793 --> 00:12:09.461
Tucker, Tucker,
come on, the rings.

00:12:09.461 --> 00:12:11.997
Oh, my God!
Tucker, did you eat the rings?!

00:12:11.997 --> 00:12:14.566
Oh, Tucker!

00:12:14.566 --> 00:12:17.836
Tucker! Tucker!
We expected more from you."

00:12:17.836 --> 00:12:20.739
The Conservative grift has been
so thoroughly discredited

00:12:20.739 --> 00:12:22.174
by the failures of
the Trump presidency

00:12:22.174 --> 00:12:23.742
that Fox has been
reduced to yelling about

00:12:23.742 --> 00:12:25.044
children's cartoons and Muppets.

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:27.012
And Trump, meanwhile,
has pinned his hopes

00:12:27.012 --> 00:12:28.614
for a political resurgence
on defending

00:12:28.614 --> 00:12:30.015
racist Confederate symbols.

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:31.950
And when they decided on
that strategy

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.385
at the Trump
campaign headquarters,

00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:36.121
I'm sure Trump went out of his
way to brag that he --

00:12:36.121 --> 00:12:37.956
-Spent some time
working on that.

00:12:37.956 --> 00:12:41.226
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:41.226 --> 00:12:43.962
-Happy birthday.
[ Laughs ]

00:12:43.962 --> 00:12:47.266
♪♪

00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:49.167 line:0%
-As New York struggles
to reopen this week,

00:12:49.167 --> 00:12:51.070 line:0%
remember that we are still
a city in crisis.

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:53.205 line:0%
And City Harvest
has been stepping up

00:12:53.205 --> 00:12:54.406 line:0%
to meet the increased need.

00:12:54.406 --> 00:12:55.608 line:0%
If you're watching this online,

00:12:55.608 --> 00:12:57.242 line:0%
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:12:57.242 --> 00:12:59.945 line:0%
Stay safe. Wash your hands.
We love you.

